# ---- 820 Welding I ----
H("820.d.1.A",3,"A student looks up the Texas community college welding certificate path, the math classes it requires and the AWS certifications that follow. She is determining:","academic knowledge and skills required for postsecondary education and careers",["only her snack order","only a movie time","only a game score"],"Know requirements before choosing a path.")
H("820.d.1.A",4,"A student aiming for a welding inspector job should plan to study:","blueprint reading, math and welding codes",["only dance","only art history","only cooking"],"Inspection careers need these skills.")
H("820.d.1.B",3,"A fab shop supervisor tells new welders that customers expect clean welds, on-time delivery and polite answers to questions. These expectations help to:","foster positive customer satisfaction",["lose customers","raise rework","reduce sales"],"Meeting expectations satisfies customers.")
H("820.d.1.B",4,"A welder who notices a defect in a finished weld before shipping should:","report and repair it before the customer receives it",["paint over it","ignore it","blame the next shift"],"Quality starts with the welder.")
H("820.d.1.C",3,"A beginning welder wears his PPE, arrives on time and follows the shop's procedures while treating coworkers politely. He is demonstrating:","the professional standards required in the workplace",["casual habits","careless habits","random habits"],"Professionalism includes respect and reliability.")
H("820.d.1.C",4,"Which habit best shows professionalism in a welding shop?","coming prepared and following procedures",["wearing flip-flops on the floor","ignoring the safety talk","leaving scrap on the floor"],"Preparation and procedure.")
H("820.d.1.D",3,"A student lists the AWS credentials she hopes to earn by graduation, then checks off the ones she already has each semester. She is evaluating:","progress toward personal career goals",["a menu","a score","a dance"],"Review progress against goals.")
H("820.d.1.D",4,"Checking progress toward a career goal each semester helps a student to:","adjust the plan and stay on track",["avoid the goal","forget the plan","skip every step"],"Progress checks guide corrections.")
H("820.d.1.E",3,"A welder asks the lead to restate the joint type, the filler metal and the inspection requirement before striking an arc on a new job. She is communicating to:","clarify objectives and expectations in the workplace",["slow the team","avoid work","confuse the lead"],"Clarify before starting.")
H("820.d.1.E",4,"If a welding procedure sheet is unclear, the welder should:","ask the supervisor before welding",["guess","skip the job","use any rod"],"Ask before welding.")
H("820.d.1.F",3,"A shop requires hearing protection near the grinders, a fire watch after hot work and a lockout/tagout before servicing equipment. These show knowledge and skills applied to:","health and safety in the workplace as specified by OSHA",["office decorating","product advertising","shift bidding"],"OSHA sets workplace safety.")
H("820.d.1.F",4,"A fire watch after welding is posted to:","make sure no sparks or hot metal start a fire later",["inspect the weld size","count the rods","check the time"],"Hot work can smolder.")
H("820.d.2.A",3,"Before striking an arc, a welder checks that the cables are not cracked, the ground clamp is secure and the work area is free of flammables. She is employing:","welding equipment according to safety standards",["equipment carelessly","equipment without checks","equipment quickly"],"Check equipment before use.")
H("820.d.2.A",4,"A frayed welding cable should be:","replaced or repaired before use",["taped and used","ignored","used outdoors only"],"Damaged cables are a shock and fire hazard.")
H("820.d.2.B",3,"A student puts used solvent rags and spent cleaning chemicals into labeled containers and sends them to a licensed hauler. She is identifying and properly disposing of:","environmentally hazardous materials used with welding",["recyclable paper","harmless water","clean scrap"],"Hazardous materials need proper disposal.")
H("820.d.2.B",4,"Used solvent from cleaning metal before welding should be:","collected for approved hazardous waste disposal",["poured in a drain","poured on the ground","thrown in the trash"],"Protect the environment.")
H("820.d.2.C",3,"A shop sorts steel, aluminum and copper scrap into separate bins that a recycler picks up each week. A student explains this to the class as part of:","the importance of recycling materials used in welding",["wasting materials","burying scrap","hiding scrap"],"Recycling conserves resources.")
H("820.d.2.C",4,"One benefit of recycling scrap metal from a welding shop is that it:","saves resources and energy compared to making new metal",["wastes energy","increases landfill","costs more energy"],"Recycling saves energy.")
H("820.d.2.D",3,"A student chooses a helmet with the correct shade lens, leather gloves, a flame-resistant jacket and safety glasses for a vertical weld. She is choosing:","appropriate personal protective equipment",["fashion items","sports gear","casual clothes"],"PPE protects from arc, heat and sparks.")
H("820.d.2.D",4,"A welding helmet lens is chosen mainly based on:","the process and amperage being used",["its color alone","the time of day","the weld's price"],"Shade number matches the arc brightness.")
H("820.d.2.E",3,"After a mock inspection, a student rates her classmates' shop practices on lockout, PPE, ventilation and fire safety and suggests fixes. She is evaluating:","skills related to health and safety in the workplace as specified by OSHA",["only the paint","only the lighting","only the music"],"Evaluate and improve safety.")
H("820.d.2.E",4,"A shop that has fumes collecting at the weld table should add:","ventilation or fume extraction",["more cutting oil","less lighting","more noise"],"Ventilation protects lungs.")
H("820.d.3.A",3,"A student studies a sketch that shows the plate sizes, the joint type and the weld symbols before cutting steel for a frame. She is demonstrating knowledge of:","welding sketches",["cooking sketches","music sketches","landscape sketches"],"Sketches guide fabrication.")
H("820.d.3.A",4,"A welding sketch is used to show:","the sizes, joints and weld types needed",["the weather","the price","the shop's hours"],"It communicates the plan.")
H("820.d.3.B",3,"On a practice board, a student labels a triangular weld between two plates at a right angle, a weld in a beveled gap and a weld through a hole in one plate. She is identifying:","types of welds such as fillet, groove, plug and spot",["types of sewing stitches","types of knots","types of paint strokes"],"Weld types differ by joint.")
H("820.d.3.B",4,"A fillet weld joins two pieces that are:","at an angle to each other, often 90 degrees",["on top of each other only","in a straight line with a gap only","not touching"],"Fillets are triangular welds at corners and tees.")
H("820.d.4.A",3,"A welder calculates how many linear feet of weld a frame needs and how much wire that will use. She is demonstrating:","mathematical skills related to welding",["only art skills","only music skills","only guessing"],"Math estimates materials.")
H("820.d.4.A",4,"A frame needs 24 welds of 6 inches each. The total weld length is:","144 inches",["30 inches","120 inches","72 inches"],"24 × 6 = 144.")
H("820.d.4.B",3,"A student writes a one-page procedure with numbered steps that another welder can follow to set up the machine and weld a lap joint. She is demonstrating:","technical writing skills related to welding",["story writing","poetry","journal writing"],"Technical writing is clear and precise.")
H("820.d.4.B",4,"A good technical procedure for welding should be:","clear, step by step and unambiguous",["vague","humorous","unfinished"],"Procedures must be followed exactly.")
H("820.d.4.C",3,"A student reads a tape measure to the nearest sixteenth of an inch and confirms the same length with a steel rule before cutting plate. She is applying:","accurate readings of measuring devices",["careless guesses","random estimates","rounded numbers"],"Accurate reads prevent scrap.")
H("820.d.4.C",4,"Reading a tape measure to the nearest sixteenth means each mark is:","1/16 inch apart",["1/2 inch apart","1/8 inch apart only","1 inch apart"],"Smallest standard tape mark.")
H("820.d.4.D",3,"A welder picks a combination square to check a 90-degree corner, a tape for length and a fillet gauge to check weld size. She is accurately using:","appropriate tools to make measurements",["the wrong tools","random tools","no tools"],"Right tool, right measurement.")
H("820.d.4.D",4,"To measure the leg size of a fillet weld, a welder uses a:","fillet weld gauge",["thermometer","stopwatch","protractor only"],"Fillet gauges check leg size.")
H("820.d.4.E",3,"A welder cuts a 3 1/4-inch piece and a 2 5/8-inch piece from a bar and adds the lengths plus a 1/8-inch cut allowance to find the total stock needed. She is solving problems using:","whole numbers, fractions, mixed numbers and decimals",["only whole numbers","only words","only guesses"],"Shop math uses fractions and decimals.")
H("820.d.4.E",4,"What is 3 1/4 + 2 5/8 + 1/8?","6",["5 7/8","6 1/4","5 3/4"],"3.25 + 2.625 + 0.125 = 6.")
H("820.d.4.F",3,"A welder converts 5/8 inch to a decimal to enter it into a calculator and converts 0.375 inch back into a fraction to find a drill size. She is performing:","conversions between fractions and decimals",["conversions of colors","conversions of music","conversions of words"],"Fractions and decimals are interchangeable.")
H("820.d.4.F",4,"The decimal equivalent of 3/8 inch is:","0.375",["0.250","0.625","0.125"],"3 ÷ 8 = 0.375.")
H("820.d.4.G",3,"A welder converts a 2-inch plate thickness into millimeters to match a drawing made in a metric country. She is performing:","conversions between standard units and metric units",["conversions of music","conversions of colors","conversions of time zones"],"Standard to metric.")
H("820.d.4.G",4,"There are 25.4 millimeters in one inch, so a 1/4-inch plate is about:","6.35 mm thick",["0.64 mm thick","2.54 mm thick","10 mm thick"],"0.25 × 25.4 = 6.35.")
H("820.d.5.A",3,"A student interviews a pipe welder, a structural welder and a welding inspector to learn about their jobs and pay. She is:","exploring careers in welding",["exploring recipes","exploring dance","exploring weather"],"Career exploration informs choices.")
H("820.d.5.A",4,"A job-shadow day with a local welding shop helps a student by:","showing real working conditions and requirements",["replacing school","hiding the job","avoiding safety"],"Real-world exposure.")
H("820.d.5.B",3,"A class studies the AWS D1.1 structural code and the API 1104 pipeline standard to see how weld quality is judged. They are understanding:","welding codes such as American Petroleum Institute standards",["cooking codes","fashion codes","game codes"],"Codes define acceptable welds.")
H("820.d.5.B",4,"The American Petroleum Institute standard 1104 mainly covers welding of:","pipelines",["bicycles","furniture","jewelry"],"API 1104 is for pipelines.")
H("820.d.5.C",3,"Given a drawing and the materials, a student cuts, fits and welds a small steel cart with only a few questions to the instructor. She is working:","independently to fabricate a variety of welded projects with minimal assistance",["only with help","only by copying","only by guessing"],"Independent fabrication.")
H("820.d.5.C",4,"Before welding a project independently, the student should:","read the drawing and check the fit-up",["guess at the sizes","skip the plan","weld without fitting"],"Plan and fit first.")
H("820.d.5.D",3,"Two students share a welding booth, one holding the fit-up while the other tacks, then they switch and inspect each other's welds. They are working:","collaboratively with other students",["alone only","against each other","without talking"],"Collaboration improves quality and safety.")
H("820.d.5.D",4,"When welding in pairs, the helper should always:","wear PPE and watch for hazards",["stand without gear","watch the arc unprotected","leave the booth"],"Safety applies to everyone nearby.")
H("820.d.6.A",3,"Before lighting a torch, a student checks for a clear area, secures the cylinders upright and has an extinguisher nearby. She is using:","safe operating practices for oxy-fuel equipment",["casual practices","careless practices","rushed practices"],"Oxy-fuel safety checks.")
H("820.d.6.A",4,"An oxy-fuel torch should never be lit with:","a match or lighter held near the tip",["a friction striker","a spark lighter","a striker made for torches"],"Use a striker, not a lighter.")
H("820.d.6.B",3,"A student chains the oxygen and acetylene cylinders upright to a cart, caps them when moving and cracks each valve slowly. She is performing:","safe handling of compressed gases",["slow cleanup","quick tidying","hurried packing"],"Compressed gas handling.")
H("820.d.6.B",4,"A compressed gas cylinder that is not in use should have:","its valve closed and its cap on",["its valve open","its cap off","no support"],"Prevents accidental release.")
H("820.d.6.C",3,"On a torch cart, a student points to the regulators, hoses, check valves, torch handle and cutting attachment and names each. She is identifying:","components of oxy-fuel gas cutting",["parts of a bicycle","parts of a camera","parts of a piano"],"Know the equipment.")
H("820.d.6.C",4,"The cutting attachment on an oxy-fuel torch adds a:","separate oxygen lever for cutting",["wire feeder","gas hose for argon","water line"],"The cutting oxygen lever delivers the cutting stream.")
H("820.d.6.D",3,"A student installs the correct tip, sets the working pressures, purges each line and lights the torch to a neutral flame. She is demonstrating:","proper set-up procedures for the oxy-fuel process",["a shutdown","a cleanup","a tool change"],"Set-up has an order.")
H("820.d.6.D",4,"Before lighting a torch, each gas line should be:","purged briefly to clear air and mixed gas",["left unpurged","blocked","filled with water"],"Purging avoids flashbacks.")
H("820.d.6.E",3,"A student finds that rusty plate, thick steel and a dull tip all change how well the torch cuts and writes down what to adjust. She is identifying:","the factors affecting oxy-fuel cutting of base metals",["factors affecting weather","factors affecting music","factors affecting cooking"],"Factors include thickness, tip size and speed.")
H("820.d.6.E",4,"Thicker steel generally requires an oxy-fuel cutting tip that is:","larger, with more heat and oxygen",["smaller","no tip","the same size"],"Thicker metal needs more heat.")
H("820.d.6.F",3,"A student pierces a hole through plate, cuts a straight line along a layout line and then cuts a bevel on an edge with the torch. She is demonstrating:","proper cutting techniques such as piercing, straight line and bevel cutting",["only sanding","only painting","only measuring"],"Cutting techniques differ.")
H("820.d.6.F",4,"To start a pierce on plate with an oxy-fuel torch, the operator should:","preheat the spot to a bright orange and then press the cutting lever",["press the cutting lever first","hold the tip very far away","use no preheat"],"Preheat before cutting oxygen.")
H("820.d.7.A",3,"Before starting a stick weld, the welder checks that the ground clamp is on clean metal, that she is standing on a dry surface and that her helmet is down. She is using:","safe operating practices for shielded metal arc welding",["careless practices","rushed practices","casual practices"],"Stick welding safety.")
H("820.d.7.A",4,"The electrode holder on a stick welder should never be placed:","on a damp or conductive surface while live",["on an insulated hook","in a rack","on a dry insulated stand"],"Live holders are hazardous.")
H("820.d.7.B",3,"A student sets up AC on one machine and DC electrode positive on another and learns how each affects arc stability and penetration. She is demonstrating knowledge of:","welding currents",["cooking temperatures","music tempos","painting styles"],"Current type affects the weld.")
H("820.d.7.B",4,"Direct current electrode positive (DCEP) generally provides:","deeper penetration",["no penetration","shallower penetration only","no arc"],"DCEP penetrates deeper.")
H("820.d.7.C",3,"A student explains that an arc between a coated electrode and the plate melts the base metal and the flux coating creates a shielding gas and slag. She is applying:","shielded metal arc welding principles",["gas welding principles","painting principles","cooking principles"],"Flux shields the weld.")
H("820.d.7.C",4,"The slag that forms on a stick weld is removed after welding with a:","chipping hammer and wire brush",["paint brush","sponge","paper towel"],"Chip and brush slag.")
H("820.d.7.D",3,"A student connects the ground, selects the amperage for a 1/8-inch electrode and checks the polarity before striking an arc. She is demonstrating:","proper set-up procedure for shielded metal arc welding",["a shutdown","a cleanup","a tool change"],"Set up before welding.")
H("820.d.7.D",4,"Amperage on a stick welder is set mainly according to:","the electrode diameter and type",["the helmet color","the time of day","the shop's name"],"Match amperage to the electrode.")
H("820.d.7.E",3,"For a mild steel lap joint, a student picks an E6013 electrode; for a structural joint on thicker plate she picks an E7018. She is determining:","appropriate electrodes for the base metal",["random electrodes","cheap electrodes","old electrodes"],"Electrodes match the job.")
H("820.d.7.E",4,"An E7018 electrode should be stored:","in a dry, heated rod oven",["in a wet bucket","outdoors in rain","in a hot car"],"Low-hydrogen rods absorb moisture.")
H("820.d.7.F",3,"A student runs fillet welds on a T-joint in the flat, horizontal, vertical and overhead positions and then welds a beveled groove joint the same way. She is performing:","fillet and groove welds in all positions",["only flat welds","only vertical welds","only tack welds"],"All-position welding builds skill.")
