H("820.d.7.G",3,"A student grinds a 30-degree bevel on each plate, cleans the edges of rust and sets a root gap before welding. She is preparing:","joints for welding",["the weld for painting","the shop for lunch","the electrode for storage"],"Joint preparation affects quality.")
H("820.d.7.G",4,"Mill scale and rust are removed from the joint before welding because they can cause:","porosity and weak welds",["better penetration","a brighter weld","a shorter arc"],"Contamination weakens welds.")
H("820.d.8.A",3,"Before pulling the trigger on a wire welder, a student checks the gas flow, makes sure the spool is secure and keeps flammables away from the area. She is using:","safe operating practices for gas metal arc welding",["careless practices","casual practices","rushed practices"],"GMAW safety.")
H("820.d.8.A",4,"The shielding gas cylinder on a GMAW setup should be:","chained upright and capped when moved",["laid flat","left unsecured","kept near the arc"],"Cylinder safety.")
H("820.d.8.B",3,"A student explains that a wire electrode fed continuously through a gun carries current to the arc while a shielding gas protects the pool. She is applying:","gas metal arc welding principles",["stick welding principles","soldering principles","painting principles"],"GMAW uses wire and gas.")
H("820.d.8.B",4,"In gas metal arc welding, the wire is:","fed automatically through the gun",["added by hand each time","not used","a stick"],"Continuous wire feed.")
H("820.d.8.C",3,"A student threads the wire through the drive rolls, sets the tension, selects the gas flow rate and adjusts the voltage and wire speed. She is demonstrating:","proper set-up procedure for gas metal arc welding",["a shutdown","a cleanup","a tool change"],"Set up before welding.")
H("820.d.8.C",4,"If the wire speed is too high for the voltage on a GMAW machine, the arc will:","stub into the plate and sound rough",["be too quiet","stop all spatter","burn the wire back instantly"],"Wire speed and voltage must be balanced.")
H("820.d.8.D",3,"For thin sheet steel a student chooses a small wire diameter with a lower voltage, and for thicker plate she picks a larger wire and higher settings. She is using:","appropriate equipment setup for the base metal in gas metal arc welding",["the same setup every time","a random setup","the cheapest setup"],"Setup depends on the base metal.")
